Inferno copy of fdlibm 5.3
==========================

Imported unmodified from the Sun/netlib fdlibm 5.3 distribution, then
reduced to what Inferno needs.  The upstream README is kept as README.

Changes made for Inferno (see the git history for the exact steps):

  - removed the build system (Makefile*, configure*), the SVID/X-Open error
    wrappers (w_*.c, k_standard.c, s_matherr.c, s_lib_version.c,
    s_signgam.c) and the functions Inferno does not use (gamma, scalb,
    significand, logb, frexp, ldexp, isnan, lgamma without _r);
    errors are reported through IEEE exceptions only;

  - every external symbol carries the fd_ prefix, so that it cannot clash
    with the host's libm:

	__ieee754_NAME   ->  fd_NAME           (fd_exp, fd_pow, fd_lgamma_r ...)
	__kernel_NAME    ->  fd_kernel_NAME    (fd_kernel_sin ...)
	NAME             ->  fd_NAME           (fd_sin, fd_floor, fd_modf ...)

    The calls that the original code made to the public sqrt() now go to
    fd_sqrt(), i.e. fdlibm's own square root; before, they were resolved
    by the host's libm.

fdlibm is written for IEEE 754 binary64 `double'; porting it on top of the
softfloat library (so that it no longer depends on the host's floating
point unit) is done in later steps.
